## Judgment on the disposition

Acceptable. A write-mode regenerate now would break the stronger standing rule
("Commit only assigned paths during concurrent work"), because the working-tree
measure/generated/ files carry 1,114 foreign changed lines. Green could not fix
F1 without committing other sessions' work, so deferral is the only correct
disposition at this point in the sequence. The deferral is honest and recorded in
both places the framework reads (the plan closeout task and the green log), and it
names the exact command and the blocking condition. The stale file is a derived
artifact; the source record (the TSV) is correct and complete at HEAD. F1 at
be89dc91 is resolved by this disposition, not withdrawn: the defect is real, its
fix is owned, and its blocker is verified.

